-- Reading CSV: the crate's `reader.rs`. The input is held in memory and
-- handed to the parser a buffer's worth at a time, as the crate's
-- `BufReader` hands it over, and each way of reading keeps its own record
-- buffers, as the crate's callers do: the line numbers in positions depend on
-- both.
